  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SDN038N PEGESMAS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description promeva:title="Description (English)" promeva:type="104" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&apos;s overall objective is to: &#x2018;&#x2019;Increase women&#x2019;s control and access to agricultural resources and markets and enable women to contribute to and benefit from improved food security&#x2019;&#x2019;. CARE aims to reach 17,306 direct individuals including IDPs and vulnerable host community members across 10 communities across two localities: Abujubeiha (Abu-Ndkina, Sambo, Karima and Tayba) and Rashad (Debaikir, Taroba, Tandik, Tajmala, Algardod, Algrewid). Our Theory of Change stipulates that changes in three outcomes are required to achieve the overall objective. Outcome 1: Improved economic opportunities and agricultural production for female smallholder farmers in mango and vegetable value chains. Outcome 2: Improved functioning of value chains and business linkages between female small-holder farmers and the private sector.  Outcome 3: Improved enabling environment for women to actively participate in more inclusive markets by addressing harmful gender norms and gender-based violence.</narrative>
  </description>
